[{"id":2430870452,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6Q5CO0","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?u=e44a465cbebabb9ea2be80b59e6dc07966bef5b7&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","login":"clayjohn","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn"},"body":"Looks good to me. I think this is a safe change because max_fps is only ever read in two places:\r\n1. The main loop (which doesn't start until well after this)\r\n2. The initialization of the Vulkan RDD\r\n\r\nWith this change we don't need to grab the `max_fps` from engine when initializing Vulkan because we can trust that it will be updated later.\r\n\r\nAccordingly, we could remove the calculation of `max_fps` and `max_time` here:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/cb411fa960f0b7fdbd97dcdb4c90f9346360ee0e/drivers/vulkan/rendering_device_driver_vulkan.cpp#L3035-L3036\r\n\r\nAnd just set the swap interval to `swap_chain->refresh_duration`","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99149#pullrequestreview-2430870452","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99149","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2024-11-12T22:42:33Z"},{"id":2431635374,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6Q78-u","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"4b94162320692770f68128581c6b99d517850421","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?u=e44a465cbebabb9ea2be80b59e6dc07966bef5b7&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","login":"clayjohn","type":"User","owned_priv